      "head_commit": {
        "id": "d28f2f713f52547af4e0ed1cbdc171e0d9fb112c",
        "tree_id": "b72370c49c22bbd367fc73869a35898af5a9b9cd",
        "message": "fix Docker builds broken by the redis-memory-server postinstall\n\nAll three images failed in CI at the deps stage. redis-memory-server is a\nworker devDependency added for integration testing; its postinstall compiles\nRedis from source, which needs 'make' — absent from node:20-alpine.\n\nPass --ignore-scripts to the workspace install in every deps stage. No image\nruns tests, so no devDependency postinstall is needed there. Verified that the\none postinstall that would matter, Prisma's engine download, is not required:\n`prisma generate` fetches the engine on demand, and the database package's\nbuild script invokes it explicitly anyway.\n\nAlso declare redis-memory-server under pnpm.neverBuiltDependencies so a plain\n`pnpm install` does not attempt the source build either; the binary is fetched\nlazily into node_modules/.cache when a test first needs it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-24T13:39:54Z",
        "author": {
          "name": "codermahbub20",
          "email": "mkrefat5@gmail.com"
        },
