        "id": "142ef70dd7c7ae21a36d2aecdbb7a797d4efa4d0",
        "tree_id": "fb71733fcf38496444dcdfb226a2a35e7c274f89",
        "message": "add GitHub Actions CI with lint, test, build, and docker jobs\n\nFour parallel jobs on push and pull_request to main, aggregated by a\nci-status job so branch protection needs one required check.\n\n- lint-and-typecheck: ESLint (newly configured — every lint script was a\n  placeholder echo, so a CI job running them would have reported green while\n  checking nothing) plus tsc across all packages.\n- test: Postgres and Redis as service containers, migrations applied, full\n  suite with coverage thresholds enforced and reports uploaded as an artifact.\n- build: production builds for api, worker and frontend, and fails if the\n  committed docs/openapi.json has drifted from the code.\n- docker-build: matrix over all three Dockerfiles with GHA layer caching,\n  build only, no registry push.\n\nTests now read REDIS_URL when set so they use the CI service container rather\nthan each suite booting its own embedded Redis — the full worker suite drops\nfrom ~90s to 39s. Locally the embedded server is still started, so a clean\ncheckout needs no setup.\n\nFixing the three real errors ESLint found: a dead initial assignment, an\nunused catch binding, and an unnecessary `this` alias.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
